W00TJj56ShtQhCVTIRX764i5-Pk2ya1rPCt_zkMPdk=", "uri": "https://mediagateway.sweet.io/media/token/XRe24Wqk/13155577461502640128/poster-image-square.png"}], "reverse_image": null}, "attributes": [{"name": "Audio Type", "value": "Sounds of the Game"}, {"name": "Date", "value": "2023-02-25"}, {"name": "Edition Number", "value": "1"}, {"name": "Moment UUID", "value": "b5c8ae77b6540000b692000000000000"}, {"name": "Play", "value": "Save"}, {"name": "Player", "value": "Andrei Vasilevskiy"}, {"name": "Rarity", "value": "Limited"}, {"name": "Series", "value": "Series 1"}, {"name": "Series UUID", "value": "b5c8ae77000000000000000000000000"}, {"name": "Set", "value": "Guardians of the Net"}, {"name": "Set UUID", "value": "b5c8ae77b65400000000000000000000"}, {"name": "Team", "value": "Tampa Bay Lightning"}, {"name": "Total Editions", "value": "500"}], "creator": {"name": "SocialSweet Inc.", "uri": "https://sweet.io"}, "description": "On a night when the Lightning faced a substantial shot deficit of 45-18, Andrei Vasilevskiy stood tall, delivering a game-saving performance with a 3-0 shutout against the Red Wings in Detroit. Late in the first period, while preserving a 1-0 lead, Vasilevskiy made his first significant save of the night by denying Tyler Bertuzzi's doorstep attempt with a remarkable left pad save. In the second period, he once again demonstrated his prowess by stopping Jake Walman's wrist shot and following it up with a right pad save. Then, in the same period, he thwarted Dylan Larkin's scoring attempt with another well-executed pad save, maintaining Tampa Bay\u2019s 1-0 lead at the time. The 3-0 victory marked one of the four shutouts Vasilevskiy achieved during the 2022-23 season.\n\nOfficially Licensed Product of the NHL, NHLPA, and/or NHLAA. All copyright, logos, and marks are the property of their respective owners and are used, under license, by Sweet. All Rights Reserved. [Terms Apply](https://nhlbreakaway.com/terms).", "edition_number": "1", "fees": [{"basis